{
  "rule": "runPipeline (empty registry, mode \"save\") — inline core semantics: wikilinks (core/wikilinks.ts), mentions (core/mentions.ts), single newline → break (remark-breaks, a Crowi core default), emoji shortcodes (remark-emoji accessible spans), link/image title & alt nullability.",
  "why": "These are the Crowi-specific inline transforms whose output shape (link nodes with hProperties.className stamps, break nodes, emoji hName/hChildren spans) both renderers must interpret identically. The single-newline break in particular is a core default (RFC-0002 Phase 5), not an extension — an implementation that renders CommonMark soft breaks diverges on nearly every page.",
  "consumers": [
    "packages/api/src/renderer/golden-corpus.test.ts",
    "apps/apple/CrowiKit/Tests/CrowiKitTests/RenderedAstGoldenCorpusTests.swift"
  ],
  "consumerContract": "The api jest driver asserts the PRODUCER side (markdown → expectedAst via runPipeline with an empty registry, and storedAst/expectedAst → expectedEnvelope via sanitizeAst). The CrowiKit XCTest asserts the CONSUMER side (its sanitize-walker mirror over storedAst/expectedAst, and its strict envelope decoder over expectedEnvelope). The Swift consumer is wired up in Phase 4 (apps/apple lives on the feature-ios-app/impl branch).",
  "normalization": "none — expected values are exact.",
  "exclusions": "Plugin-dispatch output byte strings (Mermaid / PlantUML / link-card / shiki generated HTML) are deliberately NOT pinned by this corpus — packages/e2e/tests/renderer-plugins.spec.ts owns that coverage against a live server. The corpus pins parser/core-transform STRUCTURE and the v1 projection schema shapes only; where a stored html node value would be a generated byte string, the case either omits expectedAst (code.json) or uses a synthetic stand-in value the projection never reads (typed-nodes.json).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "wikilink-absolute",
      "why": "a [[/absolute/path]] wikilink becomes a plain link node (url = target, title:null, empty data object) — no broken marker",
      "markdown": "See [[/wiki/setup]].",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "See "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "url": "/wiki/setup",
                "title": null,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "/wiki/setup"
                  }
                ],
                "data": {}
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "See "
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "/wiki/setup",
                  "title": null,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "value": "/wiki/setup"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "wikilink-display",
      "why": "[[Page|Display]]: the display text becomes the link text; a non-absolute target is broken (url \"#\", className wikilink-broken)",
      "markdown": "[[Page|Display]]",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "url": "#",
                "title": null,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Display"
                  }
                ],
                "data": {
                  "hProperties": {
                    "className": "wikilink-broken"
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "wikilink-broken",
      "why": "non-absolute targets are never resolvable links: url \"#\" + data.hProperties.className \"wikilink-broken\" so clients can dim them",
      "markdown": "[[not-absolute]]",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "url": "#",
                "title": null,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "not-absolute"
                  }
                ],
                "data": {
                  "hProperties": {
                    "className": "wikilink-broken"
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "mention",
      "why": "@username becomes a /user/<username> link with className \"mention\"; surrounding text is split around it",
      "markdown": "ping @alice please",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "ping "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "url": "/user/alice",
                "title": null,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "@alice"
                  }
                ],
                "data": {
                  "hProperties": {
                    "className": "mention"
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " please"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "ping "
                },
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "url": "/user/alice",
                  "title": null,
                  "data": {
                    "hProperties": {
                      "className": "mention"
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "value": "@alice"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": " please"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "single-newline-break",
      "why": "a single newline inside a paragraph becomes a break node (Crowi core default; GitHub-compatible) — the parent spec calls this out as the core divergence a second parser gets wrong",
      "markdown": "line one\nline two",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "line one"
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "line two"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "line one"
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "line two"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "emoji",
      "why": "emoji shortcodes resolve to a Unicode text node wrapped for a11y: data.hName \"span\", hProperties {role:\"img\", ariaLabel}, hChildren with the emoji text",
      "markdown": "done :tada:",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "done "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "🎉",
                "data": {
                  "hName": "span",
                  "hProperties": {
                    "role": "img",
                    "ariaLabel": "tada emoji"
                  },
                  "hChildren": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "value": "🎉"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "done "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "🎉",
                  "data": {
                    "hName": "span",
                    "hProperties": {
                      "role": "img",
                      "ariaLabel": "tada emoji"
                    },
                    "hChildren": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "value": "🎉"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "link-title",
      "why": "link.title is string-or-null per @types/mdast — a present title must be preserved verbatim",
      "markdown": "[home](/home \"Home page\")",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "title": "Home page",
                "url": "/home",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "home"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "image-inline-alt-title",
      "why": "an image with inline siblings stays a phrasing image node (no crowiFigure); alt and title are preserved",
      "markdown": "before ![alt text](/img.png \"Title\") after",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "before "
              },
              {
                "type": "image",
                "title": "Title",
                "url": "/img.png",
                "alt": "alt text"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " after"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
